# NEVER NORMALISE LINE ENDINGS. Several artefacts in this project are sha256
# manifests consumed by POSIX tools on data produced elsewhere, and a manifest's
# line endings are part of the manifest: a CRLF manifest makes `sha256sum -c` read
# a carriage return into every filename and fail on all of them, while a checker
# written in Python -- which reads in universal-newline mode -- reports success.
# The checker and the checked sharing a blind spot is not a passing test.
* -text
